{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["And these are the judgments — let those who know understanding know and understand that I have not come to explain halakhot, even though they are the essence, as I explained in Genesis. For from the superfluity of verses the aggadot and halakhot are derived, and some of them will be found in the commentary of Rabbenu Shlomo, my mother's father, of blessed memory. And I have come to explain the plain sense of the verses, and I shall explain the laws and halakhot according to the way of the world. And even so, the halakhot are the essence, as our Rabbis said: halakhah uproots the plain sense. — 'For six years he shall go out in the Jubilee,' and there are those who draw a distinction between them."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The final sentence appears to cite or allude to a halakhic dictum or verse; the Hebrew reads לשש שנים יצא ביובל, which may reflect a truncated or variant quotation. Transmitted hyper-literally without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:42:18.520947271Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}